hich idea clearly applies to stated problem.\nSolves identified problem directly related to stated problem (do X to get Y, and Y is part of stated problem). Yes, meets logging mandate. So 4.\n\nEvidence: The module directly records operational events and satisfies Article 12(2)(a)-(c) logging requirements for deployed high-risk systems.\n\neffectiveness (1-4): degree to which idea will solve problem.\nReasonable and will solve stated problem without regard for workability. Will it solve? It provides traceability automatically. Probably 4.\n\nEvidence: If implemented, automatic event capture with Article 12 categories would provide lifetime traceability and post-market monitoring required by the Act.\n\nacceptability (1-4): degree to which idea is socially legally politically acceptable.\nCommon strategies that violate no norms. 4.\n\nEvidence: Building internal telemetry for compliance aligns with legal requirements and does not offend sensibilities.\n\nimplementability (1-4): degree to which idea can be easily implemented.\nEasy to implement at low cost, or non-radical changes? Eight-week sprint pairs one engineer and one data scientist on existing metrics pipeline. Some changes, reasonably feasible measures -> 3? Or easy? Might be some changes. Could be 3 = some changes, or reasonably feasible measures.\n\nEvidence: The plan relies on an existing metrics pipeline and a small two-person sprint, making deployment feasible though it requires engineering effort.\n\nPossibly 4 = easy to implement at low cost? Eight weeks maybe not trivial. I'll pick 3.\n\nNeed output format: echo id exactly. For each subscale give <subscale>_evidence then <subscale>.\n\nProbably JSON? Return rating. Provide lines.\n\nLet's output:\n\nid: P2196\nparadigm_relatedness_evidence: ...\nparadigm_relatedness: 2\n...\n\nMake sure order listed.\n\nProceed.",
