le and will solve stated problem without regard for workability? Probably solves main problem of meeting logging mandate and adapt R&D. Could be 4 = reasonable and will solve stated problem without regard for workability (if you could do it, it would solve main problem). Yes.\n\nApplicability: degree to which idea clearly applies to stated problem. Solves identified problem directly related. Do X to get Y, and Y is part of stated problem. Yes 4.\n\nParadigm_relatedness: degree to which idea preserves or modifies paradigm anchored to this problem.\n4 = paradigm breaking: introduces new elements AND changes relationship between lab's R&D and its compliance obligations, or addresses larger problem of what lab researches\n3 = paradigm stretching: changes that relationship (e.g., logging woven into science, new partners or offerings born from compliance)\n2 = slightly paradigm stretching: introduces new elements (tools, formats, processes) but still treats compliance as logging practice\n1 = paradigm preserving\n\nProposal introduces single event bus serving research dashboards, compliance archive, post-market monitor simultaneously. Logging woven into science. Changes relationship? It weaves logging into R&D pipeline. Might be paradigm stretching: changes that relationship. Could be slightly paradigm stretching: introduces new elements but still treats compliance as logging practice. The text says one infrastructure investment serves three regulatory obligations and internal experimentation simultaneously, avoiding double maintenance. That's weaving logging into science. I'd say 3 = paradigm stretching.\n\nOriginality: degree to which idea is not only rare but also ingenious... Not expressed before AND ingenious? Single event bus for research and compliance is unusual but not extremely surprising; common in microservices. Might be interesting. Could be 2 = interesting. Or 3 = unusual, interesting; shows some imagination. Probably 2? Event sourcing for ML is known. I'd r