ach system still lacks. That is gap analysis not full implementation. But also instruments. Might be partial. I'd say 3 = reasonable and will contribute to solution, it helps but only partial solution (since mapping identifies lacks). Could be 4. Hmm.\n\nThe text: \"identifying which event types, timestamps, and reference-database pointers each system still lacks. The platform team instruments...\" So both identification and instrumentation. Might solve problem. Probably effectiveness 3? If you could do it, it would solve main problem? Might need more than six weeks. I think it's reasonable and will contribute, but maybe not fully guarantee compliance for all systems. I'd give 3.\n\nLet's output format: echo id, then each subscale evidence sentence then score.\n\nNeed <subscale>_evidence then <subscale>.\n\nProbably JSON? It says return rating echoing its id exactly. For each subscale... give \"<subscale>_evidence\" first and then \"<subscale>\". Provide likely as lines.\n\nI'll output structured:\n\nid: P1077\nparadigm_relatedness_evidence: ...\nparadigm_relatedness: 2\n...\n\nMake sure one sentence evidence.\n\nLet's craft sentences.\n\nparadigm_relatedness_evidence: The proposal adds log emitters and schemas but keeps compliance as a logging practice layered onto existing pipelines without changing how R&D relates to compliance. Score 2\n\noriginality_evidence: Retrofiting pipelines with regulatory log schemas is a common compliance engineering response that labs routinely propose. Score 1\n\nimplementability_evidence: It uses existing Kubernetes clusters, experiment tracker and object store with no new hardware in a six-week sprint, indicating low-cost non-radical change. Score 4\n\nacceptability_evidence: Instrumenting pipelines for mandated logging is a standard, norm-conforming compliance measure that violates no legal or business sensibilities. Score 4\n\napplicability_evidence: Mapping training and inference pipelines to Articles 12(1)-(3) directly addresses the mandate to enable automatic event logging and traceability. Score 4\n\neffectiveness_evidence: Adding structured log emitters will improve traceability but the sprint is framed as mapping gaps and a modest upgrade, so it contributes to rather than fully guarantees Article 12 compliance. Score 3\n\nReturn.\n\n",
