e) first and then <subscale> (integer). Probably JSON? Return rating. Likely list.\n\nProvide evidence sentences.\n\nLet's craft:\n\neffectiveness_evidence: The redesign secures long-term retrievability of logs but does not generate the event logging content mandated by Article 12(2)-(3).\neffectiveness: 3\n\napplicability_evidence: It directly addresses the Article 12(1) lifetime retention requirement central to meeting the logging mandate.\napplicability: 4\n\nparadigm_relatedness_evidence: It introduces new storage tools and processes while keeping compliance as a separate logging practice rather than changing R&D-compliance relationship.\nparadigm_relatedness: 2\n\noriginality_evidence: Centralized long-term retention with tiered cold storage and a compliance query API is a common, mundane IT compliance approach.\noriginality: 1\n\nimplementability_evidence: Provisioning tiered cold storage, automated ingestion and a retrieval API requires coordinated IT work but is reasonably feasible for an R&D lab.\nimplementability: 3\n\nacceptability_evidence: Building compliant archival infrastructure violates no legal, social or business norms.\nacceptability: 4\n\nReturn.\n\n",
