y output like:\n\nid: P2859\nparadigm_relatedness_evidence: ...\nparadigm_relatedness: 3\n...\n\nLet's do that.\n\nMake sure evidence one sentence.\n\nParadigm_relatedness evidence: The proposal weaves Article 12 logging into existing experiment-tracking and reproducibility workflows, changing how R&D and compliance interact. Score 3.\n\nOriginality evidence: Unifying compliance logs with publication reproducibility metadata via a single ontology is unusual for labs facing Article 12 and shows imaginative integration. Score 3.\n\nAcceptability evidence: Aligning internal documentation with legal traceability and scientific norms violates no laws or sensibilities and is socially expected. Score 4.\n\nImplementability evidence: Redesigning pipelines, mapping fields to notebooks/version control and quarterly audits require moderate engineering changes but are reasonably feasible. Score 3.\n\nApplicability evidence: The proposal directly addresses the mandate to technically allow automatic recording of Article 12 events by reusing existing tracking systems. Score 4.\n\nEffectiveness evidence: If implemented, dual-purpose logging would provide the required timestamps, database references, matched inputs and verifier IDs while eliminating duplicate effort. Score 4.\n\nReturn.\n\n",
