onably feasible. Could be 3. Not easy low cost? Maybe requires effort but feasible. I'd say 3.\n\nParadigm_relatedness (1-4): degree preserves/modifies paradigm anchored to this problem.\nParadigm preserving: standard compliance and logging practice; lab's way of working unchanged. Audit is standard compliance. So 1.\n\nOriginality (1-4): degree not only rare but ingenious...\nCommon, mundane, boring. Gap audit is common. Score 1.\n\nCheck definitions: originality 1 = common, mundane, boring. Yes.\n\nReturn rating echo id exactly.\n\nNeed format: For each subscale give \"<subscale>_evidence\" then \"<subscale>\".\n\nProbably JSON? The prompt says return rating... echo its id exactly. For each subscale in order give ... Probably output lines.\n\nLet's produce:\n\nid: P1216\napplicability_evidence: ...\napplicability: 4\n...\n\nEnsure one sentence evidence.\n\nMake sure each evidence is one sentence.\n\nProceed.",
