ce relationship.\n\nacceptability (1-4): degree socially legally politically acceptable.\nCommon strategies violate no norms. Assigning overhead, scoring proposals is acceptable. Score 4.\n\nEvidence: Internal budget allocation and portfolio review criteria are normal management practices that do not violate laws or sensibilities.\n\nimplementability (1-4): degree can be easily implemented.\nSome changes or reasonably feasible measures = 3. Or easy? Requires revising funding model, quarterly reviews. That's some changes. Probably 3.\n\nEvidence: Implementing a revised intake scoring rubric and a fixed fifteen percent overhead line requires process change and buy-in but is administratively feasible.\n\nReturn JSON with id and subscales.\n\nNeed output format: echo id exactly. For each subscale give <subscale>_evidence sentence then <subscale> integer.\n\nProbably produce lines.\n\nLet's output:\n\nid: P2732\napplicability_evidence: ...\napplicability: 4\n...\n\nEnsure one sentence evidence.\n\nMake sure sentences end with period.\n\nProceed.",
